Russ Berger wrote:

> Mingzuo Shen wrote:
>
> > Hi,
> >
> > I'd appreciate any answers to this. We just got our
> > 8400s a couple of days ago. The 8400s are hooked into VT510s.
> >
> > >>> show config | more
> > This does not work. The error message was something like
> > there was an invalid character in basic mode.
> >
> > >>> show *mode*
> > >>> set console_mode ?
> > >>> set console_mode advanced
> > >>> show config | more
> > still does not work
> >
> > >>> show
> > There is no "prompt" variabe?
> > I'd like to set P0>>> to something meaningful like PRD>>>
> > and QA>>>
> >
> > While I was editing some file using vi in haste,
> > I was dropped from Digital Unix 4.0D to the firmware console!
> > The error messages appeared on the screen along with the text
> > I was editing. The error messages said processor 1 halted,
> > processor 2 *not* halted, ... The only way I knew was to
> > type "boot".
> >
> > I didn't notice what key I typed. I was using vi, in a hurry to
> > go home for the day.
> >
> > What key I probably used?
> > How to prevent that?
> > How to continue after seeing P0>>>?
> > On Sun Sparcs, if the PROM prompt ("ok") appears by accident,
> > typing a "go" sometimes can get the Sparc back to Unix.
> >
> > Many thanks in advance!
> > Mingzuo
>
> 1. To get into advanced command mode at the console prompt:
> P00>set mode advanced
> then commands like "show config |more" will work.
> 2. The P00> prompt means cpu0 is the primary cpu now. "set cpu 7" would
> change prompt to P07>>>.
> 3. When you have a direct serial connection to the 8400 you have console
> access, and even when the OS is booted, ^p gets interpreted as interupt
> to console and brings system down to console command level. Type
> >>>continue or just >>>c and it will be back up without missing a beat
> (well cpu cycles would have been suspended for a few seconds).
> NOTE: it machine hangs, type ^p, then >>>crash to generate a crash dump.
> Maybe it will tell you what hung the system. Look at
> /var/adm/crash/crash-data.n for the crash analysis after reboot.
> --
> Russ Berger
> Technical Account Manager
> Business Critical Support Team       Russell.Berger@digital.com
> Digital Equipment Corporation






