Hi! I learned something new about mutexes the other day. I had thought that
if the location of the mutex was in a memory region visible to multiple
processes, that it would be usable by those multiple processes. I found out
that I was mistaken.

After flailing around for a while, I discovered the PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED
mutex attribute. Shortly after that, I found that Digital UNIX 3.2G does not
support this (apparently optional) attribute. Digging a bit further, I found
in the 4.0 documentation that it is not supported there, either.

What is the appropriate substitute? I know that I can use the System V IPC
semaphores to do this, but mutexes are so much simpler....

Thanks!

