Ganesh Thiagarajan  <cethia@unix1.sncc.lsu.edu> wrote:
>
>I am running OSF on DEC Alphastation. My program is
>running out of stacksize.
>
>When I set the limit using the command
>
>limit stacksize unlimited
>
>it only goes to 32MB maximum. There is 512 MB RAM that is
>available. 
>
>Any suggestions to increase this limit is greatly appreciated.

Sounds like there is a hard limit set. The hard limit is the
"maximum," you can raise your soft limit only until it reaches
the hard limit. Only the superuser can raise a hard limit (though
a luser may lower it, irreversible without killing and restarting
the process, in this case logging out and in again). The -h switch
to limit works with hard limits. Thus, limit -h stacksize will tell
you the hard limit for stacksize. It's probably set in a login.conf-
type file somewhere.

