Asgar Ali wrote:
> 
> Sorry,
> 
> the triple free(ptr) did not work on this DEC system.
It's not supposed to. According to the ANSI C standard (4.10.3.2), if
the space has been deallocated by a call to free or realloc, the
behavior is undefined. In Digital Unix, the allocator does return memory
back to the system if it is able to. Most C allocators do not. 

