N Madden <n.madden@ucc.ie> writes:

> 	I'll looking for a good (and free for eductional use) mail program to
> run under Digital Unix. Currently, some user use pine but thats rather
> unfriendly to folk who've just moved from Eudora. Netscape mail is good,
> but rather clunkey. VM is excellent but not everyone likes using xEmacs.
> And dxmail is pretty basic and also can't POP from a remote server it
> seems. 
> 
> 	What else if out there and where can I get it?

I use exmh. It is free with a very nice GUI interface to mh written in
Tcl/Tk and quite well supported. Lots of MIME and pretty good PGP
support. PGP is limited to 2.6.2, although I expect to see 5.0 support
soon. (Several people have been working on it.)

You can get exmh from http://www.beedub.com/exmh/. I also recommend
replacing mh with nmh from http://www.math.gatech.edu/nmh/. It will
also use (if present) a large number of other free tools. This is
discussed at the web site.
