! @(#)$RCSfile: template.pcf,v $ $Revision: 1.1.2.3 $ $Date: 1997/05/06 12:57:23 $
!
! NOTE: Do not modify this file!
!       This file will be replaced when the operating system is updated.
!+
! This template documents the Printer Control File (PCF) format and is
! intended for use as a reference guide.
!
! Digital does not support user created PCF files.
!
! PCF files are utilized by the /usr/lbin/pcfof print filter. The PCF files
! enable the pcfof filter to work with many types of printers. Creating a PCF
! file requires familiarity with the printer's programming language.
!
! Special characters used in PCF files are:
!	!     - Indicates a comment.
!	\xxx  - Specify a character by octal value. eg: \033 represents the 
!	        character escape. The value must be three digits.
!	\\    - Enter a single backslash character.
!	/     - A slash as the first character in a field definition
!		indicates a file specification.
!
! Entries are in the format fieldname:fieldvalue, where fieldname is a
! specific printing property as listed in this template and fieldvalue is a
! value expressed as a number, a character, a string or a filename.
! For example:
!
! reset:<string> specifies the character or string of characters that will be
! sent to the printer. For example, if the printer's reset value is the
! escape character followed by 'E', this would be specified as `reset:\033E'.
! The fieldvalue is comprised of all the characters between the colon
! character and the end of the line. The fieldvalue must not contain the null
! character octal code \000.
!
! Types of fieldvalues are:
!	<string>	Multiple characters starting after the colon to the 
!			end of the line.
!	<file>		Directory path and filename starting from /.
!	<string/file>	Specify a string or file specification. Not both.
!			A string value must not start with a /.
!	<number>	An unsigned integer value.
!	<character>	Any single character except \000.
!	<Y/N>		The character Y for yes or N for no.
!
! For properties that are listed as "printer dependent", refer to the
! printer manufacturer's document for presence of the feature and value
! necessary to use it.
!
! Preliminary testing can be performed without the use of a printer. Place a
! copy of the pcfof filter, PCF file, and a test file in the same directory.
! Example command to test a new.pcf file:
!
!	cat test_file | pcfof -ntest +L +C./new.pcf > a.out
!-

! format version:003
!	PCF file format revision level.  Do not change.
!
!	Field is required.

! filter type:<string>
!	Specifies the printer mode and filter for input data. Values are:
!
!	PPL	to process text files containing DEC ANSI control sequences.
!	PCL	to process text files containing HP PCL control sequences.
!	ASCII	to process plain text files (no control sequences).
!	XF	to pass the file unprocessed (no formatting at all).
!		In XF passthru mode printer setup is still performed.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is required.

! auto passthru:<Y/N>
!	Specifies if the filter should detect pre-formatted files. When the 
!	value is Y and the file contains a printer reset, and accounting is 
!	not specified, the file will be sent to the printer unprocessed. 
!
!	Default value: N
!	Field is optional.

! locale:<string>
!	Specifies the I18N locale.
!
!	Field is optional.

! reset:<string>
!	Specifies the command to reset the printer into a known state.
!
!	Value for DEC ANSI:	\033[!p
!	Value for PCL:		\033E
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! reset delay:<number>
!	Specifies the time to wait, in seconds, before continuing to print.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! init seq:<string>
!	Specifies additional printer characteristics such as: line truncation, 
!	font type, horizontal character pitch, vertical line pitch.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! init delay:<number>
!	Specifies the time to wait, in seconds, before continuing to print.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! term seq:<string>
!	Specifies the printer characteristics to set after the file has 
!	completed printing. Minimally this field contains the same value 
!	as `reset:'.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! term delay:<number>
!	Specifies the time to wait, in seconds, before continuing to print.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! auto reset:<Y/N>
!	Specifies if the filter should reset the default page orientation 
!	and trays before printing the `term seq:' command.
!
!	Default value: N
!	Field is optional.

! font file prefix:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file to send before printing the font file.
!
!	Field is optional.

! font file suffix:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file to send after printing the font file.
!
!	Field is optional.

! font file:<string/file>
!	Specifies the font string or font file to print.
!
!	Field is optional.

! font file lines:<number>
!	Specifies the number of lines `font file:' printed.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! prefix page1:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file to print prior to printing page 1.
!	Eg: Place the company logo on the first page of a document.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! prefix page1 lines:<number>
!	Specifies the number of lines `prefix page1:' printed.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! prefix pagen:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file to print prior to printing each page
!	starting with page 2. 
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! prefix pagen lines:<number>
!	Specifies the number of lines `prefix pagen:' printed.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! suffix page1:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file to print on the bottom of page 1.
!	Eg: Print for `Company Name Internal use Only' on the footer of page 1.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! suffix page1 at line:<number>
!	Specifies the line number to start printing `suffix page1:'
!	string or file.
!	Note:	Subtract the greater of `suffix page1 at line:' or `suffix
!		page2 at line:' from portrait lines:' and `landscape lines:'
!		to ensure there is enough room on the page to print the data.
!
!	Field is required when `suffix page1:' is defined.

! suffix pagen:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file to print on the bottom of each page 
!	starting with page2.
!
!	Field is optional.

! suffix pagen at line:<number>
!	Specifies the line number to start printing `suffix pagen:'
!	string or file.
!	Note:	Subtract the greater of `suffix page1 at line:' or `suffix
!		page2 at line:' from portrait lines:' and `landscape lines:'
!		to ensure there is enough room on the page to print the data.
!
!	Field is required when `suffix pagen:' is defined.

! character map file:<string/file>
!	Specifies the string or file that contains information on converting 
!	a single character to an alternate character or character string.
!	The file format requires only one assignment per line. For example:
!	
!	! 	Convert all [ characters to {.
!	[:{
!	! 	Convert all 2 characters to the string `two'.
!	2:two
!	! 	Convert all @ characters to the string `test'
!	\100:t\145st
!
!	The colon character `:' must be the second character in the
!	assignment. Note that \100 is treated as one character. 
!	A comment line is an exclamation point followed by a space.
!
!	Field is optional.

! orientation:<string>
!	Specifies the default page orientation. The available options are
!	portrait or landscape.
!
!	Field is optional.

! portrait:<string>
!	Specifies the command to set the printer in portrait orientation.
!	Portrait is when the page height is greater than the page width.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! portrait lines:<number>
!	Specifies the maximum number of lines that can be printed on a page
!	in portrait orientation. 
!
!	Default value: 66
!	Field is optional.

! portrait columns:<number>
!	Specifies the maximum width in characters that can be printed on a
!	page in portrait orientation. A value of 0 indicates no page width
!	restrictions. A value of 0 will only work when pw is set to 0 in the
!	/etc/printcap file.
!
!	Default value: 80
!	Field is optional.

! landscape:<string>
!	Specifies the command to set the printer in landscape orientation.
!	Landscape is when the page height is less than the page width.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! landscape lines:<number>
!	Specifies the maximum number of lines that can be printed on a page in
!	landscape orientation.
!
!	Field is required when `landscape:' is defined.

! landscape columns:<number>
!	Specifies the maximum width in characters that can be printed on a
!	page in landscape orientation. A value of 0 indicates no page width
!	restrictions. A value of 0 will only work when pw is set to 0 in the
!	/etc/printcap file.
!
!	Default value: 132
!	Field is optional.

! landscape threshold:<number>
!	Specifies the width, in characters, the filter should change the page
!	orientation from portrait to landscape. If the value is 0 no automatic
!	switching is performed.
!
!	Default value: 81
!	Field is optional.

! wrap line:<Y/N>
!	Specifies if a line exceeding the portrait or landscape column value
!	should be continued on the next line. A value of N will cause the 
!	line to be truncated.
!
!	Default value: N
!	Field is optional.

! wrap line mark:<string>
!	Specifies the string to print when the current line has been continued
!	on the next line. The printed result must print only one character.
!	This character will be used to indicate the current line exceeds the
!	page width and the remaining text has been continued on the next line.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! newline:<string>
!	Specifies the command to set the printing position to column 0 and 
!	advance 1 line. Suggested value: \015\012
!
!	Field is required.

! return:<string>
!	Specifies the command to set the printing position to column 0.
!	Suggested value: \015
!
!	Field is required.

! newpage:<string>
!	Specifies the command to eject the current page and set the printing 
!	position to line 1 column 0 on the next page.
!	Suggested value: \015\014
!
!	Field is required.

! eojnewpage:<string>
!	Specifies the command to conditionally eject the last page in the 
!	file only when printable data exists. Using this option can cause 
!	accounting to be off by one page.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field value is optional.

! backspace:<character>
!	Specifies the character to move the printing position back 1 character.
!
!	Default value: \010
!	Field is optional.

! tab:<character>
!	Specifies the character that indicates a tab.
!
!	Default value. \011
!	Field is optional.

! tab width:<number>
!	Specifies the number of characters between tab positions.
!
!	Default value 8.
!	Field is optional.

! tab expansion:<Y/N>
!	Specifies if the tab character should be replaced with spaces to 
!	advance to the next stop.
!
!	Default value: N
!	Field is optional.

! indent:<number>
!	Specifies number of spaces to indent each line in the user's file. 
!	Does not apply to strings or files specified in this file.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! banner utility:<file>
! trailer utility:<file>
!	Specifies the program to create a banner or trailer page. The programs
!	are called with the following parameters:
!		-xh	Print header page
!		-xt	Print trailer page
!		-n 	User name
!		-h 	Host name
!		-N 	Job name
!		-j	Job number in the queue
!		-C	Job class name
!		-s	Spooling directory
!		-w	Page width
!		-l	Page length
!	The name of the utility must end in _ps if the utility creates
!	postscript banner pages.
!
!	Program is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! banner tray:<string>
!	Specifies the tray name to select for printing the banner page.
!	The available tray names are defined below via `input tray <name>:'.
!	Should only be used when `input tray default:' has been specified.
!
!	Field is optional.

! trailer tray:<string>
!	Specifies the tray name to select for printing the trailer page.
!	The available tray names are defined below via `input tray <name>:'.
!
!	Field is optional.

! input tray default:<string>
!	Specifies the tray name to select for printing the file. The command
!	`lpr -I' can override the default selection. The available tray names
!	are specified below via `input tray <name>:'.
!
!	Field is optional.

! input tray <name>:<string>
!	Specifies the name of a tray and the command to select it. For example, 
!	`input tray upper:\033&l1H' creates the input tray name `upper' for
!	use by `banner tray:', `trailer tray:', `input tray default:' and the
!	`lpr -I' command. A maximum of 25 input tray names can be defined.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! output tray default:<string>
!	Specifies the tray name to select to place the printed pages. The 
!	available tray names are defined below via `output tray <name>:'.
!
!	Field is optional.

! output tray <name>:<string>
!	Specifies the name of a tray and the command to select it.
!	A maximum of 25 output tray names can be defined.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! sides:<number>
!	Specifies the number of sides to print on each sheet.
!	Set to 1 for single sided (simplex) printing or 2 for two sided 
!	(duplex) printing.
!
!	Default value: 1
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! simplex:<string>
!	Specifies the command to select single sided printing.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! duplex:<string>
!	Specifies the command to select two sided printing.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! define <name>:<string>
!	Specifies the name of an option and the command to select it. For 
!	example, `define economode:\033(s1Q' creates the option `economode'.
!	The option is invoked by using `lpr -O<name>'. Example: lpr -Oeconomode
!	A maximum of 25 options can be defined.
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! ps enable:<string>
!	Specifies the command that will switch a multi-language printer into
!	PostScript mode. A command must be specified to activate the following
!	ps definitions.
!
!	Suggested value for autosensing printers: %!\012
!	Suggested value for HP PJL printers:
!		\033%-12345X@PJL ENTER LANGUAGE=POSTSCRIPT\012
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is optional.

! ps enable delay:<number>
!	Specifies the time to wait, in seconds, before continuing to print.
!
!	Default value: 0
!	Field is optional.

! ps disable:<string>
!	Specifies the command to reset the printer.
!
!	Suggested value for autosensing printers:\004
!	Suggested value for HP PJL printers: \004\033%-12345X
!
!	Value is printer dependent.
!	Field is required when `ps enable:' is defined.

! ps disable delay:<number>
!	Specifies the time to wait, in seconds, before continuing to print.
!
!	Default value:0
!	Field is optional.

! ps prolog:<file>
!	Specifies the file to print after the `ps enable:' command.
!
!	Field is optional.

! ps portrait:<string/file>
!	Specifies the command to set the printer in portrait orientation.
!
!	Field is optional.

! ps landscape:<string/file>
!	Specifies the command to set the printer in landscape orientation.
!
!	Field is optional.

