In article <01bd7832$416b7060$33a18e81@NT.Guidegruppen.dk>, "Henrik Lykke Christensen" <hlc@guidegruppen.dk> writes:
>
>Hi.
>Do any know the default blocksize on digital unix filesystem.
>Is it 1K 2K 4K 8K or something else.

Which file system?  There are two read-write file systems to
choose from (UFS and AdvFS) and one read-only file system
(ISO-9660).

For both UFS and AdvFS the answer is 8 KB and it can't be
changed.  UFS does support 4 KB block size file systems
created on ULTRIX.  For UFS you can check the block size
by using the dumpfs command and looking at the bsize field.

I don't know where the page size for AdvFS is documented, but
it is probably somewhere.

Given the default parameters both file system will attempt to
allocate data as contigously as it can and on sequential reads
will attempt to use fairly large I/Os while doing read-ahead.

