> Warning: More than one file named 'CCC_InfosPln.cc' found in the binary.
> Warning: Breakpoint not set
>
> Any clue somebody ?

Without any more information, I'd guess that you're using a newer C++
compiler and you've got a source file with several template definitions.
If this is NOT the case, then please report the problem to the Ladebug
team, because we'd like to know about it.  (To report a problem, it really
helps to know exactly which version of Ladebug, the compiler, and the
operating system you're using.  It also helps to have a small code
example.)

If it is the problem, it's a known bug that we're trying to find a fix
for.  The difficulty is that the compiler is producing symbol table
information separately for each template - which provides more than one
"file" contribution in the binary.  This confuses Ladebug.  The solution is
to make Ladebug smarter, make the compilers produce more consumable symbol
table information, or some combination of the two.

For some simple cases, you may be able to work around it by moving the
template definitions into their own separate files.  (Ladebug, for example,
is written in C++, has a lot of templates, is compiled with one of the
latest compilers, and does not demonstrate this problem as far as we know.
We use Ladebug to debug itself.)
