Matt,

You need to get the system to the console prompt. In order to do this
you need to
crash it using the reset switch (next to the power switch).  You can
also just power
cycle the system.  (Depending on how the system is configured, you can
also try
typing CNTL-P at the CDE login. This may get you to the console prompt.)

If the system is not set to autoboot, you should come to the console
prompt, blue
screen with >>> .  If it is set to autoboot you need to stop it prior to
entering
the boot sequence by typing CNTL-C while it is completing the power on
self test
(the blue screen with the countdown e9.e8.e7.e6...).  You should be able
to catch
and stop the boot sequence and be at the console prompt.

At the console prompt type "boot -fl s" for singleuser.

At the singleuser # prompt type the command bcheckrc which does an fsck
and mounts
local filesystems from the fstab file.  You will be able to use vi at
this point
in line edit mode, but it may work in screen mode if you set your
teminal type
to vt100.

Regards,

Rocky



