> Now, under 4.0d, when a non-root user attempts to do this, it
> fails, giving the following message:

>    mount: Can't load cdfs module

Under 4.0D, CDFS is now a dynamically loadable module. You can make
it static by putting it into the kernel config file. So just put a:

options         CDFS

in your /sys/conf/MACHINE file and rebuild the kernel.

