Actually, real programmers never allocate memory from the kernel
at all (in part because they do not like to share their hardware
with somebody else's program, and kill the kernel as soon as they
can lay their hands on the console switches). Real programmers 
use statically dimentioned arrays, and retype the object code 
with the new size by hand when the old limit is exceeded. In this 
way, that pesky problem with releasing memory is avoided altogether.

