We added one to a Unix machine. 

At the machine level check that the device is 
there and on the same channel as the other one. 
(I can't suggest how this will look on your machine)
This is the part where the machine should automatically 
recognize it. 

Kernel changes: 

Change the system config file and rebuild the kernel. 
Add a line(s) to the config file like the lines for the 
other NIC card, but with the correct device number, and 
channel if the channel is different. You might also need to 
check that the channel is also defined in the config file 
if it is different from the exiting one. 




