Scott Patterson wrote:
> 
> I am trying to add a PCI network card to an Alpha 2100 running OSF1 v4.  The
> reseller tech support tells me I should just install the card and it should
> be recognized.  neither ifconfig and netconfig see it.  This is the first
> time I have tried to add a NIC to an Alpha.
> 
> Am I missing something here?
> 
> Scott

What kind of NIC?

I recently installed a DE500-AA 10/100 card on an AlphaServer 2000 
4/233 running DUNIX 4.0a . It would not show up until I changed the
"ew*0_mode" setting at the SRM console. By default it sets to AUI 
(which will not work for a twisted-pair card):

	>>> show ew*0_mode

	Will display the current mode for the device

	>>> set ew*0_mode "type"

	* = NIC letter. First NIC is a, second is b, and so one.
	type = "aui" for AUI or Thinwire (10BASE-2), "twisted-pair"
		for 10BASE-T.

Check the firware manual for more detailed info. Once it is set in
firware and an "init" or power cycle is performed, you should be ready
to go. A sizer and/or kernel rebuild might be necessary (not sure. It's
been awhile).

Hope that helps a little... 

Until soon...
