Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Michael,

    After the card is added, you need to rebuild the kernel.  Here are the steps I
use.

1) Shutdown the system
    shutdown now
    sync
    sync
    halt

2) Install new card
    show device  (before adding card)
    Note MAC addresses and ewa0 and ewb0.  Depending on how the
    system "reads" the bus, the cards could show up in a different
    order (i.e. the card that was in the system could show up as
    the second card - ewb0).

    Add card
    show device (after adding card)

3) Rebuild kernel
    boot -fi genvmunix
    doconfig

4) Reboot with new kernel
    cp /vmunix /vmunix.old
    mv /sys/HOSTNAME/vmunix /vmunix  # HOSTNAME is `hostname` in caps

5) Configure NIC
    uerf -Rr 300 | more
        You should see a tu0 and tu1.
    netsetup
        You should now be able to see the new NIC card.



Thanks,

Brent



