From: ericferg@aol.com (EricFerg)
Subject: [Fix] Re:  Should a DU4 Patch Run for over 8 Hours???
Date: 1998/05/07
Message-ID: <1998050711522700.HAA24365@ladder03.news.aol.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 351076375
X-Admin: news@aol.com
Organization: AOL http://www.aol.com
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Our problem is fixed now.  To a DEC tech support guy who replied to my original
message, it appeared that our 51 MB patch (either the original TAR file, or
some of the files that were extracted from the TAR file) was corrupted.

The DEC guy recommended that we:

- Do a CKSUM against the patch TAR file on our Backup server and the one on the
Primary (the box whose patch was giving us trouble) to make sure the patch file
we put on the Primary wasn't corrupted during the download from DEC ...

- (Checksums matched, so ...) Interrupt the DUPATH process (using good old
Ctrl+C)

- Restore the root ( / ) and /usr filesystems from our latest backup

- Boot w/ the last good kernel

- Extract the patch files from the TAR file again

- Try the patch again ...

This time, the patch worked ... and it only took about 30 minutes!

Thanks for everyone's help & suggestions ...

Capt Ferguson



